  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d9e80177-bd20-4041-8f38-349858ad598f",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1264,
        "content": "## NKSC_CyberIncidents\n\n[Watch the Loom walkthrough](https://www.loom.com/share/bbe3d346324441e7ace1c059489507bb)\n[GitHub](https://github.com/syn-con/nksc-nivs-integration-example)\n\nThis template is an example workflow demonstrating how to use the **NKSC NIVS n8n community nodes**. It is intended as a reference implementation that can be adapted to your own incident source, field mappings, authentication, and response handling.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Receives an incoming request through a Webhook and checks whether incident fields are provided directly or in an uploaded file.\n2. If a file is provided, extracts and parses its contents, then merges the resulting incident fields into a consistent payload.\n3. Routes the payload to the appropriate NKSC NIVS node: initial warning, minor incident, major incident, or near miss.\n4. Checks the NIVS response for errors and immediately returns an error response if the submission fails.\n5. If successful, returns either a JSON response or converts the result to a downloadable file.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n* [ ] Configure **When Nivs Incident Webhook Called** to match your own source system and authentication requirements.\n* [ ] Ensure incoming requests contain either direct incident fields or a supported XLSX file.\n* [ ] Configure credentials settings for each **NKSC NIVS** submission node.\n* [ ] Verify **Extract Incident Data from File** uses the expected XLSX file and binary property.\n* [ ] Adjust **Parse Incident Fields from File** to match the field names and structure used by your source system.\n* [ ] Test the response paths and modify them as needed for your integration.\n\n### Customization\n\nThe surrounding webhook, parsing, routing, and response logic is provided only as an example of how the NKSC NIVS nodes can be integrated into an n8n workflow. Replace or modify these parts to fit your own system and use case.\n\n### Requirements\n\nThis example uses the `@synergyconsulting/n8n-nodes-nksc-nivs` community node and is intended for self-hosted n8n instances only. Install and configure the community node before importing or running the workflow.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
